==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Best mobility fruit in the game (four mobility abilities).
* Good for avoiding and escaping fights.
* Great for PvP.
* Unpredictable attack patterns (land and sky mobility).
* Great counter to [[Instinct]]'s player detection as moves such as [X], [C], and [V] make the player disappear from the area. However, if the enemy has [[Pale Scarf]], they can usually also detect players on other islands.
* Great for [[guns|gun]] or [[Swords|sword]] mains.
* Great for chasing an enemy who has better mobility than the user. (E.g. [[Light]], [[Tiger]], [[Phoenix]])
* Most reliable source for finding [[Legendary Sword Dealer]], [[Barista Cousin]] and [[Elite Pirates]] as well as [[Fruit Notifier|Fruit Hunting]].
* All moves have minor stun damage.

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* Good mobility.

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Good stun.
* Good AoE.
* Amazing [[Combos|combo]] starter.
* Can grab players even if they have [[Instinct]] activated.

|{{Ability|X}}
*Completely negates delayed damage moves, such as Sanguine's C move or Kitsune's Z move
* Extremely abusable stun, especially since the user is un-detectable.
* Makes the user invisible/invincible for a short period of time, and also unable to be detected by [[Instinct]].
** Completely negates [[water]] damage.
* The duration is unaffected by [[Races#Version 3|V3]]/[[Races#Version 4|V4]] abilities, [[Flash Step]], etc. as these won't make the user exit. (Because they count as individual moves.)
* Can be used to punish charge moves like [[Dark Blade]] {{Ability|Dark Blade|X}} (hold) or [[Godhuman]] [C] (hold).
* Good for escaping combos ([[Instinct|Instinct-Trick]] and use, or time it).

|{{Ability|C}}
* The best mobility move in the entire game.
* Can teleport to almost any island in the current sea.
* Extremely useful for transportation.
* Great for boss hopping.
* Good for chasing [[Portals]] runners ([[Portals]] in the [[Third Sea]]), as the user can teleport to their location behind their back.
* Quite good for escaping Bounty Hunters.
** Allows the user to run to any area (like the [[Sea of Treats#Cake Land|Cake Land]]) and hide or run until they can teleport to a Safe Zone.
* Very useful when doing sea events. (If an ally dies, the Portal user can spawn a portal, which allows the player to "teleport")

|{{Ability|V}}
* High damage to [[NPCs]].
* Large hitbox.
* Can be used to trap flying exploiters. (Everything that tries to fly out or fall from the flat platform will be instantly teleported into the center)
* Great for dealing against runners.
* Great combo potential due to its large hitbox and all players who are in the dimension will be forced out of it after the user leaves it.
* Good for hiding, as the user can use {{Ability|C}}, hide, and then use {{Ability|V}} to escape.
* Can get rid of [[Terrorshark]]s or any [[sea event]] by having all players of the [[Sea Exploration Group]] enter the portal.

|{{Ability|F}}
* Easy to grind with.
** Can do massive damage if stacked in the right way (infinite loop).
* Can be used to confuse and displace players.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Not recommended for fruit mains for PvP due to having long cooldowns, lack of [[Area of Effect|AoE]] and overall low damage, except for the {{Ability|Z}} ability.
** Easily countered by [[Blade]] if both players are [[sword]] users.
* Mainly close-ranged attacks.
* Requires very precise aiming and timing.
* Not recommended for [[Sea Beast]] hunts for [[fruit]] mains because of low damage.
* High mastery requirements for [[First Sea]] and early [[Second Sea]] players.

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* No damage.
* Can be annoying, as it could fling the user while grinding.

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Can be hard to hit in PvP without stun or at long range.
* Short range.
* Mostly focuses on one target, making it less viable for grinding [[Enemies|NPCs]].
* Can easily be [[Instinct]]-tricked, allowing the opponent to escape a potential combo.

|{{Ability|X}}
* Can be hard to hit in PvP without stun.
* A well-timed [[Buddha]] {{Ability|Buddha|F}} can drag the player out of the ability.
** On rare occasions, other well timed attacks may pull the user out too (ex: [[Godhuman]] {{Ability|Godhuman|Z}})
* Bosses can snipe the user as soon as the user exits. (This can be countered by using a different move.)

|{{Ability|C}}
* Long startup, the user has to wait 2 seconds before getting teleported upon activation.
* Very low damage.
* The portal stays for a while, making it easy for players to catch up.

|{{Ability|V}}
* Low damage to players.
* Most exploiters can somehow disappear or move non-stop and can still kill the user if they are not careful. Most of them will find a way to turn off the PvP to reset.
* Drains a small amount of [[energy]] over time.
* Only useful on players, although it still does damage and brings [[Enemies|NPCs]] to the dimension, but they glitch out.
* Cannot be used in [[Friendly PvP]] without leaving the arena.
* When the opponent exits out of the portal, they gain i-frames for one second, so the user won't be able to do combos after they get out of the portal.

|{{Ability|F}}
* Damages enemies slowly.
}}
</tabber>

