==Trivia==
* When the Portal dimension is used while having no stats in melee, the player can stay in the dimension forever due to the low energy drain being so low.
* The teleport abilities do not teleport other players if they have PvP disabled or if they are in a Safe Zone and are not allied to the user.
* Portal is the first fruit that has a teleport move that other players can access.
* Although Portal and [[Phoenix]] share the Robux price of 2,000, they do not share the same money value. Portal is valued at {{money|1,900,000}}, while Phoenix is valued at {{money|1,800,000}}.
** This is the first pair to share the same Robux price but not the same value, the second pair being [[Control]] and [[Kitsune]]. Both are priced at 4,000, but Control is valued at {{money|9,000,000}}, while Kitsune is valued at {{money|8,000,000}}.
* Portal is the first fruit that is able to bring up a separate GUI.
* The old Portal C UI was shared with Door's C UI, until it was reworked in Update 27.0
* Alongside the teleport move, Portal has the most mobility moves at four. Phoenix is second at three.
* The permanent version of Portal has a lot of value, mostly because of its [C] World Warp move, as it can teleport nearly anywhere.
* [[Midnight Blade]] and [[Bizarre Revolver]] create portals similar to those created by Portal.
* None of Portal’s moves have destructible physics.
* The portals once appeared sideways due to a bug. It is unknown why it occurred, but as of now the bug has been patched. However, the user can still make a sideways portal by somehow glitching and making themselves underground until their body is sideways, then using [C] World Warp, and the portal will be sideways.
* [[Raids]] seem to teleport players to the raid islands through portals similar to the ones created by Portal.
* Portal is the only blox fruit to be Octagon shaped.
* If the Player uses the Divine Portal skin, its '''[V] Dimensional Rift''' will make an different ambient sound while in the dimension compared to its Default skin.
;{{Ability|TAP}}
* Can be used to glitch through some walls (E.g.: The igloo entrance on the cold side of [[Hot and Cold]] in the [[Second Sea]]).
* Used to have the shortest cooldown at 2–2.5 seconds, but it has since been nerfed to 3.5 seconds.
* This move is buffed slightly in the [[dungeons]] lobby.

;{{Ability|X}}
* When using this ability and passing through {{Ability|C}} from the enemy, the invisible duration will reset upon teleportation, causing the user to become invisible again.

;{{Ability|C}}
* The user can teleport to the [[Cursed Ship]] without reaching [[Levels|Lv]]. 1000 through the use of this move. However, the enemies do not drop [[Ectoplasm]]s. The user will still be able to talk to the [[NPCs|NPC's]], also the [[Cursed Captain]] will not drop the [[Hellfire Torch]] to the player, and they will not be able to accept any [[Quests]] (because of the level requirement).
* This is a great move for escaping Portal {{Ability|V}} loopers as this move cannot be canceled when used no matter what damage is taken.
* This move could actually deal damage, even to the user. However, the amount of damage dealt was 1 damage or less, which is also why when the user teleported through the portal, the [[health]] bar on the top right appeared instead of being hidden.
* This move could teleport the user out of a [[raid]] and still keeps the timer. This means if the raid was beaten, they would still be awarded the [[fragments]] even if they did not actively participate in the raid. When outside the raid, the user was immune to the attacks of other players. (This has been patched in {{Update|26.8}})
* While the GUI (menu) is open, players can use moves and [[Air Jump]]/[[Dashing|Dash]] freely, whereas before [[Update 27.0]], players were unable to do anything except walk and jump only once.
* If a player uses this ability then dies, the portal will constantly teleport the player's remains (pieces shattered after dying), meaning upon respawning, the player will be constantly teleported to the target location.
* If used on lower-end devices it can cause lag from being constantly teleported from both ends of the portal.
* Portal's C move can be used as a "Admin Killer Combo," when the user teleports someone to Hot and Cold in [[Second Sea]] and use the Hallow Scythe to launch them into the lava which will kill them almost instantly. This can also be done with swords other than Hallow Scythe that have moves that knockback players.

;{{Ability|V}} 
* There's a bug that could happen by someone letting the player enter {{Ability|V}} and then immediately quit the game. This leads to players being able to turn off fog, which effectively helps to clarify vision.
* If the player is launched out of the dimension through the top portal by a high-knockback move, such as [[Godhuman]] {{Ability|Godhuman|C}}, a bug may cause them to end up in a void far away from the islands.
* Sometimes, when the dimension despawns and a player is in it, they will fall from the sky, high above the islands.
* During a Terrorshark Event, the user can use {{Ability|V}} to cancel the Event (note: if theres other people, they have to join too or the event wont be canceled)

;{{Ability|F}}
* The user can use this to "swap places" with an enemy. However, if they use this when the enemies are really close to them, they will be at the portal where the user exits.
* The portals can still be used while in the void from {{Ability|X}}, which means that the user can use this move for transporting/escaping quickly on the battlefield.
* It can be opened up at any position and distance between each other, so the user can essentially trap [[NPCs]], [[bosses]] or players in a loop dealing massive damage to them along with the minor [[stun]] damage dealt from entering the portal until the portal closes.
* Since it is an instant teleport move, it can be used to clip through walls, such as the [[Temple of Time]], allowing players to view the outside of the temple.

